WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:05.910
We all know that it doesn't pay to gamble,
but a week ago, I heard a paradox that seems

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:10.230
to show the opposite- that you can earn money
whenever you gamble.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:14.490
Let me show you how it works for a particular
game- but after I'll show you it generalises

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:15.490
to any.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:18.940
The game I heard it in the context of is Roulette.

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:24.020
Apparently there's a way to play the game
where you just need to guess either black

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:27.449
or red- both have an equal probability.

00:00:27.449 --> 00:00:31.920
You bet a certain amount of money and if you're
right, they give you the amount you betted.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.640
If you lose, you pay them.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:34.640
Simple.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:38.079
So convince yourself that this is a game of
pure chance, if you played this game a lot

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:40.800
you wouldn't expect to win or lose anything.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:45.030
By the way, if you played this in a real casino
the odds are slightly against you so that

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:49.860
they make money- but that doesn't make a big
difference to this paradox so let's look at

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:52.210
the fair game for now.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:55.610
It seems like there is nothing you can do
to improve the chance you make money.

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:58.190
But let’s think about this strategy.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.500
What if you said, I'll always bet red.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.350
First time I'll bet 2.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:04.070
If I win, I'll stop.

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:06.659
Otherwise I'll play again but this time I'll
bet 4.

00:01:06.659 --> 00:01:11.070
And if I lose again I'll bet 8, etc, etc.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.740
Then say you win on the 3rd round.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:17.140
You win 8, which covers all your previous
loses.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:22.510
The beauty of this is, you will win eventually,
and whenever that is, you win back everything

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:25.570
you lost and then some.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:30.700
You might say, yeah but the amounts of money
you're betting every time get huge quickly.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:32.170
And that's true.

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:35.930
But it's pretty unlikely you'll even lose
many times in a row.

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:40.230
The probability you'll lose 3 rounds is 1
in 8.

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:45.380
The idea behind this strategy is to chase
your losses- you know, that thing that people

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:47.290
tell you never to do.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:54.640
If you lost 3 rounds then you've lost 2+4+8=14.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:57.330
So you bet 2 higher than that total loss.

00:01:57.330 --> 00:02:02.930
That means that if you win this round, you
get back everything you lose, and 2 more.

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:06.801
You can check this yourself but this works
for what ever round you finish up on, you

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:09.920
bet your total losses so far plus 2.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:14.360
So whenever you play this game, as long as
you go through until you eventually win a

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:17.079
round, you always make 2.

00:02:17.079 --> 00:02:21.590
But this seems like a contradiction- you aren't
supposed to consistently make money playing

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:22.590
this game.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:25.180
You're supposed to break even.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:29.669
It gets worse than that, because you can apply
this strategy to any betting situation, now

00:02:29.669 --> 00:02:31.409
matter the odds.

00:02:31.409 --> 00:02:34.629
You just bet a little bit more than all your
total losses so far...

00:02:34.629 --> 00:02:40.609
But wait, before you bet on your house, you
can see that this is clearly stupid for most

00:02:40.609 --> 00:02:42.700
betting situations.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:46.109
Most of the time, bets are stacked well against
you.

00:02:46.109 --> 00:02:50.529
Let's say you're playing a game where you
have a 1/10 chance of winning each bet -which

00:02:50.529 --> 00:02:52.799
is not at all unrealistic.

00:02:52.799 --> 00:02:59.030
Then the chance you'll lose even 12 games
in a row is still very high, about 30%.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:04.889
But at that point you'll have to spend about
$8000 and still are likely to lose more.

00:03:04.889 --> 00:03:09.469
So yeah, don't actually go do this in real
life please.

00:03:09.469 --> 00:03:14.250
This stratergy doesn't actually work- it's
obvious why not when the odds are like this,

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:20.150
but when the odds are 50/50, like in the roulette
game, it's hard to see what the problem is.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:21.879
That's where the paradox is.

00:03:21.879 --> 00:03:25.299
I'm going to give you a week to see if you
can figure it out.

00:03:25.299 --> 00:03:29.999
It took me a lot of frustrated hours with
a friend until we cracked it, but it was good

00:03:29.999 --> 00:03:32.650
fun to think about which is why I wanted to
tell you guys.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:35.510
It's a very interesting paradox.

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:40.469
And if you do figure it out, here are some
other variations you might try.

00:03:40.469 --> 00:03:46.219
What if you decide not to be too greedy, and
you only bet your total loss plus 1 each time,

00:03:46.219 --> 00:03:47.659
instead of 2?

00:03:47.659 --> 00:03:52.819
Or what if you get super greedy, and you bet
your loss plus some growing amount?

00:03:52.819 --> 00:03:57.439
In those two scenarios, see how quickly the
amount you bet grows, and what your expected

00:03:57.439 --> 00:03:59.700
winnings are.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:02.760
If you need some hints, I have some small
ones in the description.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:04.040
Good luck.

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:07.700
Try it with a friend so you can discuss it-
I highly recommend it.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:11.369
Oh and, promise me one thing- that you won't
go gamble this week.

00:04:11.369 --> 00:04:11.560
Thank you.

